---
interface Props {
  name: string;
  abbr: string;
  slug: string;
  regionLabel: string;
  taxRate: number;
  cities: { name: string; slug: string; zip: string }[];
}
const { name, abbr, slug, regionLabel, taxRate, cities } = Astro.props;
const nonContiguous = ['hawaii', 'alaska'].includes(slug);
const noTax = taxRate === 0;
const cityList = (cities || []).slice(0, 6);
---
{nonContiguous && (
  <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-amber-300 dark:border-amber-700 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 mb-2">Why shipping to and from {name} costs more</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-900/90 dark:text-amber-100/90 leading-relaxed">
      {name} sits outside the contiguous 48 states, so every package travels part of the way by air or ocean freight.
      UPS and FedEx primarily use <strong>air services</strong> to reach {abbr}  -  standard Ground is limited or unavailable  -  so their rates run well above mainland Ground.
      <strong>USPS is usually the most affordable option</strong> to and from {name}: Priority Mail and Ground Advantage use flat, zone-based pricing regardless of the air leg, and Priority Mail <strong>Flat Rate boxes ship for one price no matter the weight</strong>.
      Many carriers also add an extended-area or Alaska/Hawaii surcharge, so expect rates roughly 2-4x higher than an equivalent mainland shipment. Always compare USPS flat-rate options first, and use the calculator above before you commit to a carrier.
    </p>
  </div>
)}

<div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Shopify Shipping from {name}: Tips for 2026</h2>
  <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
    <p><strong>Use Shopify Shipping discounts.</strong> Merchants selling from {name} get up to 88% off USPS and up to 77% off UPS retail rates through Shopify Shipping  -  well below counter prices, which matters most on longer {regionLabel} routes where every zone bump adds cost.</p>
    <p><strong>Set a free-shipping threshold that covers your zone.</strong> Most Shopify stores use a $50 - $75 free-shipping minimum. Check what a typical order actually costs to ship from {name} with the <a href="/free-shipping-threshold/" class="text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 hover:underline font-medium">free shipping threshold calculator</a> before you lock in a number.</p>
    <p><strong>{name} sales tax on shipping.</strong> {noTax ? `${name} has no statewide sales tax, so you generally do not collect tax on orders shipped within ${name}  -  one less thing to configure in your Shopify tax settings.` : `${name}'s base statewide sales tax is ${taxRate}%. Whether the shipping charge itself is taxable depends on how you present it on the invoice, so set your Shopify tax rules for ${name} accordingly.`}</p>
    <p>Sourcing the product before you ship it? <a href="https://supply-rank.com/" class="text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 hover:underline font-medium">SupplyRank</a> lists verified wholesale suppliers so your landed cost  -  product plus shipping from {name}  -  stays competitive.</p>
  </div>
  {cityList.length > 0 && (
    <div class="mt-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">Shipping rates by city in {name}</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-3">Pick a city for a calculator with live USPS zone lookup from that ZIP code:</p>
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {cityList.map((c) => (
          <li><a href={`/shipping/${slug}/${c.slug}/`} class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 text-xs text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 hover:border-teal-500 hover:text-teal-700 dark:hover:text-teal-400">{c.name} ZIP {c.zip}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  )}
</div>

<div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-6">More Shipping Questions  -  {name}</h2>
  <div class="space-y-5">
    <div class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 pb-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">How long does shipping from {name} take?</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Transit time from {name} depends on distance (your USPS zone). USPS Ground Advantage delivers in 2-5 business days and USPS Priority Mail in 1-3 business days. UPS Ground and FedEx Ground take 1-5 business days  -  nearby {regionLabel} states arrive in 1-2 days, while cross-country shipments take 4-5. For guaranteed dates, UPS/FedEx air and USPS Priority Mail Express deliver in 1-2 days at premium rates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 pb-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">Is there a weight or size limit for packages shipped from {name}?</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">USPS Ground Advantage and Priority Mail cap out at 70 lb and 130 inches in combined length + girth. UPS and FedEx Ground accept packages up to 150 lb and 165 inches length + girth, with a maximum length of 108 inches. Packages over 50 lb, longer than 48 inches, or with a longest side over 96 inches usually trigger UPS/FedEx "Additional Handling" or "Large Package" surcharges  -  factor these in when you set your {abbr} shipping rates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 pb-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">What items are restricted or add surcharges when shipping from {name}?</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Hazardous materials (aerosols, perfumes, nail polish), lithium batteries, and flammable liquids face restrictions and hazmat fees with every carrier; standard commercial goods ship without issue. The most common avoidable surcharges are dimensional-weight pricing on large-but-light boxes, additional-handling fees on oversized items, and residential-delivery or fuel surcharges from UPS and FedEx. USPS charges no residential or fuel surcharge, which often makes it the cheaper choice for small parcels from {name}.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pb-2">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">What tools help calculate shipping costs from {name}?</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Use the calculator at the top of this page to compare live USPS, UPS, FedEx, and DHL rates from {name} by weight and destination zone. For international orders, add customs duties and taxes (DHL and UPS provide landed-cost estimators). If you're still sourcing the product you're about to ship, <a href="https://supply-rank.com/" class="text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 hover:underline font-medium">SupplyRank</a> helps you find verified wholesale suppliers so your landed cost  -  product plus shipping  -  stays competitive.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
